      'it rapidly evaluates incoming sensory information for danger by two routes a fast crude low road straight from the thalamus that can trigger a response before you consciously know what the stimulus is and a slower detailed high road through the cortex when it detects a threat it drives the fear response freezing the startle reflex autonomic arousal racing heart sweating stress hormone release through the hypothalamus and hpa axis and heightened attention and vigilance',
